  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Evidence Fund: A plurilateral approach, implications for South Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The current geo-political and economic context is seeing a breakdown of consensus and the undermining of global multilateral institutions. This research will explore whether building consensus and co-operation through a plurilateral approach is viable, and if it would contribute to economic development for LDC and other developing countries, with a focus on South Africa.

This research project will develop recommendations for where South Africa could effectively and strategically use a plurilateral approach. The research will be beneficial and provide insights to the South African Department of Trade, Industry and Competition, for the upcoming WTO ministerial (MC 14) where plurilaterals are included in the discussion.</narrative>
  </description>
